  "name": "Molokan singing (Russian Spiritual Christian psalms, California)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Unaccompanied sacred singing of the Molokans, Russian Spiritual Christians who reject icons and instruments, brought to California by families who began emigrating from the Transcaucasus in about 1904 and settled on Potrero Hill in San Francisco and in the Boyle Heights 'Flats' of Los Angeles. Psalms and spiritual songs in Russian are begun by a song leader and taken up by the whole congregation in slow, richly ornamented heterophonic part-singing; Sidney Robertson Cowell recorded singing and preaching at the Russian Molokan Church on Potrero Hill in 1938 for the WPA California Folk Music Project.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1900s molokan singing, ritual Devotional, christian gospel branch. same melody all voices. country church. small-diaphragm pencil condenser, portable field-recorder pre. tape 15ips.",
